# Copy into rtl/lint_allow.yaml (optional - only when a warning is real and
# justified; see skills/vde/reference/remediations/LATCH.md before reaching
# for this file on a LATCH finding specifically - allowlisting one is
# almost never the right call). Every entry needs `rule` and `reason`;
# check_lint.py refuses an entry missing either, it does not silently drop
# it. Narrow it with `file` and `signal` (or `line`): a rule-only entry
# waives that rule everywhere and is reported as `lint_broad_waiver`, and an
# entry that matches no warning fails lint as `lint_stale_waiver`.

- rule: <VERILATOR_RULE_NAME>
  file: rtl/<file>.v
  signal: <the name the warning quotes>
  reason: <why this specific warning is not a defect here>
